# Assembly surface for 15.3.39--40

`source_lemma_15_3_39` proves `L = ⟨L^S⟩` by constructing the two-factor
projections and applying the commutator contradiction. `source_lemma_15_3_40`
proves `Y₊ ≤ L`: the remaining component/centralizer split, in either plane
orientation, gives an A₄ actor and an actual A₄-square equivalence for Y,
contrary to 15.3.9.

The conditional source inputs are the genuine earlier local, component and
action conclusions in `ContainmentSourceInputs`; their discharge belongs to
the parent assembly. The corrected three-part reduction of 15.3.37 is used
throughout, and the literal alternatives follow only after containment.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.39--40, printed pp.1137--1138.
-/
